abstract: >-
  A macroeconomic regime-detection and asset-allocation pipeline built to real-time
  standards: point-in-time data aligned to each series' publication lag,
  forward-filtered hidden Markov state probabilities, and expanding-window
  re-estimation, with tests that check the absence of look-ahead directly. It
  compares regime strategies with a rebalanced 60/40 portfolio over 535 months,
  runs a factorial ablation that restores three forms of look-ahead bias, and
  measures statistical power: detecting a 0.1 Sharpe ratio improvement at 80%
  power requires between 128 and 610 years of monthly data, depending on the
  correlation between strategy and benchmark.
keywords:
  - regime switching
  - hidden Markov models
  - backtesting
  - statistical power
  - Sharpe ratio inference
  - look-ahead bias
  - tactical asset allocation
  - reproducibility
